<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Innioasis Updater CE Notice Feed Markup Specification
  Hosted at: https://innioasis.app/notice.xml

  Displays on-screen hint toast announcements to users of the app.
  
  Fields:
  - id: required, unique string identifier for the notice.
  - persistent: boolean ("true" | "false", default: "false").
      * "false" (or omitted): Non-persistent notice. When dismissed by the user,
        it is permanently dismissed and will not return on the next app run.
      * "true": Persistent notice. It will return on every app launch, even if
        dismissed during a prior run.
      * CACHE INVALIDATION: If the remote notice.xml contents change from the
        locally cached file on the user's computer, the new file is automatically
        loaded and the updated notice is shown, even if previously dismissed.
  - severity: "info" | "warning" | "critical" (default: "info").
  - from: optional ISO date YYYY-MM-DD. Shown on or after this date.
  - until: optional ISO date YYYY-MM-DD. Shown on or before this date.
  - models: optional comma-separated list of target models (e.g. "Y1,Y2"). Omit for all models.
  - platform: optional comma-separated list (mac,windows,linux). Omitted means all.

  Contextual targeting (all optional; every attribute set must match):
  - device_type: comma-separated hardware revisions, e.g. "A" or "B" ("Type A"
      is accepted). Y1 is the only model with revisions today.
  - firmware_repo: the repository the notice is about, written exactly as in
      slidia_manifest.xml, e.g. "rockbox-y1/rockbox". Full GitHub URLs are
      accepted and * wildcards work.
  - firmware_version: comma-separated release tags, e.g. "v3.2.0", "v3.2.*"
      or "*" for any release of that repository. The leading "v" is optional.

  A notice with none of these is for EVERYONE. In Updater CE the Select
  Software card shows one notice at a time, ordered by how specific the match
  is (firmware_repo, firmware_version, device_type, models, everyone) and
  cycles through the rest of what applies; a reader's contexts are the current
  selection plus every device logged for update reminders. Here on the site,
  notices.html?repo=<repo>&model=<Y1|Y2>&type=<A|B>&version=<tag> lists notices
  about that firmware first while keeping everyone's notices in the same list.
  The app's Notices list, pop-out list and notification tray always show every
  active notice, with no contextual narrowing.

  The inline card above the release list on firmware.html is narrower still:
  it only shows a notice whose severity is warning, severe, alert or critical
  AND that sets firmware_repo or firmware_version, so the list is interrupted
  only by a problem that names the build on screen. Every other notice stays
  in the bell tray and on notices.html.

  Child elements:
  - <title>: required, headline of the notice.
  - <content>: required, short banner description/body text (also supports <body>).
  - <full_content>: optional, the extended body. Markdown is supported: headings,
      bullet/numbered lists, **bold**, *italic*, `code`, fenced code blocks,
      quotes and horizontal rules, [links](https://example.com) and images such as
      ![a screenshot](https://example.com/screenshot.png). It is shown on the
      notice's own page (notices.html?notice=<id>) and in the app's notices list.
      Falls back to <content> when omitted.
  - <url>: optional page for the notice. A URL that is only the bare site root
      (https://innioasis.app with no page) is ignored, and the notice links to
      its own page instead.
  - <link>: optional URL alias for backwards compatibility with earlier builds.
-->
<notices updated="2026-11-07">

  <notice id="2026-11-07-codesigning" persistent="false" severity="info" from="2026-10-25" until="2026-12-31" models="Y1,Y2">
    <title>Windows 10/11 app launch issues reported</title>
    <content>Users are reporting that they are unable to launch the app - find out more here.</content>
    <full_content>We're aware an issue where Microsoft Endpoint Protection and Smart App Control are blocking launches of our app. This has been reported to Microsoft asa false-positive and we are awaiting registration with SignPath so we can sign our builds and avoid these false-positives in the future.<br>A temporary workaround is to Open Settings > Privacy & Security > Windows Security > App and Browser control > Smart App Control > Evaluation. This will allow you to open the app.<br>Do not set Smart App Control to "off" as you will not be able to turn it back "on" without re-installing Windows.<br>We're hoping this will be resolved as rapidly as the false-positive was applied to our application.</full_content>
    <link>https://innioasis.app</link>
  </notice>

</notices>
